      "writtenOn": "2022-12-14T06:36:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Are you sure VPNs send null interfaces? I think production code (as opposed to test code) should never be announcing null interfaces. Some of our tests do though I think.\n\nAs for the logging - this log is disabled by default so I wouldn\u0027t particularly optimize for it. I think it\u0027s better to unindent and simplify the code.\n\nIf you really want to log the case where the interface is null, maybe you can do that in its own log line? Something like:\n\n    if (iface \u003d\u003d null \u0026\u0026 mtu !\u003d 0) {\n        if (DBG) log(\"setting MTU with null interface: \" + nai);\n        return;\n    }",
      "parentUuid": "e60c8c4e_9082a670",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3118,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 3122,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "a423e63302873b07c657bdace63ab6375cedb50e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c3a780c0_df9f614d",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 3122,
      "author": {
        "id": 1966927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-14T08:46:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, I believe after switching to an underlying network with no internet, the VPN IKE session is lost and it sends LPs with null interfaces, expecting the initial interface to go down. Is it a bug then? (see https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:frameworks/base/services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/Vpn.java;l\u003d3701?q\u003dVpn.java)\n\nIs the `loge` below (line 3140) disabled by default or do you mean the `if (VDBG)` is disabled by default? \n\nThere is already a log line for the case where the interface is null (line 3140).\nBefore this CL, the log line will be skipped when the MTU is identical. Simplifying the code does not maintain that behaviour. Do you think it should not maintain that behaviour? Do you think I should change the `loge` to your suggestion instead?",
      "parentUuid": "62135e39_443163b9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3118,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 3122,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "a423e63302873b07c657bdace63ab6375cedb50e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "56725352_4cde0e16",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 3122,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-14T10:20:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ouch. Yes, I see. It does that when it has no tunnel interface but wants to remain connected. Once Lucas\u0027s changes are in to allow the default network to remain null while the VPN is connected, I think we can just have the VPN disconnect its agent completely instead of setting a null interface. But until that happens, I suppose we\u0027ll need to support it.\n\nThat said - does the code I suggest behave identically to the current code other than what messages it logs? If so, I think we should prefer code simplification/readability over keeping the logging the same as it was before - especially since VDBG is by default false unless the user runs an adb command to set it to true.",
      "parentUuid": "c3a780c0_df9f614d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3118,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 3122,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "a423e63302873b07c657bdace63ab6375cedb50e",
